<ReportItem port="22" svc_name="ssh" protocol="tcp" severity="2" pluginID="900101" pluginName="OpenSSH &lt; 9.6 Multiple Vulnerabilities" pluginFamily="Misc.">
<plugin_type>remote</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>Medium</risk_factor>
<cvss3_base_score>5.9</cvss3_base_score>
<cvss3_vector>CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N</cvss3_vector>
<cvss_base_score>4.3</cvss_base_score>
<vpr_score>6.1</vpr_score>
<exploit_available>true</exploit_available>
<cve>CVE-2023-48795</cve>
<cve>CVE-2023-51385</cve>
<synopsis>The SSH server running on the remote host is affected by multiple vulnerabilities.</synopsis>
<description>According to its banner, the version of OpenSSH running on the remote host is prior to 9.6. It is therefore affected by multiple vulnerabilities, including a prefix truncation weakness in the SSH transport protocol (Terrapin).

Note that Nessus has not tested for these issues but has instead relied only on the application's self-reported version number.</description>
<solution>Upgrade to OpenSSH version 9.6 or later.</solution>
<see_also>https://www.openssh.com/txt/release-9.6
https://terrapin-attack.com/</see_also>
<plugin_output>
  Version source    : SSH-2.0-OpenSSH_8.9p1 Ubuntu-3ubuntu0.1
  Installed version : 8.9p1
  Fixed version     : 9.6
</plugin_output>
</ReportItem>
<ReportItem port="443" svc_name="www" protocol="tcp" severity="3" pluginID="900102" pluginName="SSL Medium Strength Cipher Suites Supported (SWEET32)" pluginFamily="General">
<plugin_type>remote</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>High</risk_factor>
<cvss3_base_score>7.5</cvss3_base_score>
<cvss3_vector>CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N</cvss3_vector>
<cvss_base_score>5.0</cvss_base_score>
<vpr_score>5.1</vpr_score>
<exploit_available>false</exploit_available>
<cve>CVE-2016-2183</cve>
<synopsis>The remote service supports the use of medium strength SSL ciphers.</synopsis>
<description>The remote host supports the use of SSL ciphers that offer medium strength encryption, including 3DES. Medium strength ciphers use key lengths of at least 64 bits and less than 112 bits.</description>
<solution>Reconfigure the affected application if possible to avoid use of medium strength ciphers.</solution>
<see_also>https://sweet32.info/</see_also>
<plugin_output>
  Medium Strength Ciphers (&gt; 64-bit and &lt; 112-bit key, or 3DES)
    ECDHE-RSA-DES-CBC3-SHA   Kx=ECDH  Au=RSA  Enc=3DES-CBC(168)  Mac=SHA1
</plugin_output>
</ReportItem>
<ReportItem port="22" svc_name="ssh" protocol="tcp" severity="1" pluginID="900103" pluginName="SSH Server CBC Mode Ciphers Enabled" pluginFamily="Misc.">
<plugin_type>remote</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>Low</risk_factor>
<cvss3_base_score>3.7</cvss3_base_score>
<cvss3_vector>CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N</cvss3_vector>
<cvss_base_score>2.6</cvss_base_score>
<cve>CVE-2008-5161</cve>
<synopsis>The SSH server is configured to use Cipher Block Chaining.</synopsis>
<description>The SSH server is configured to support Cipher Block Chaining (CBC) encryption. This may allow an attacker to recover the plaintext message from the ciphertext.</description>
<solution>Disable CBC mode cipher encryption, and enable CTR or GCM cipher mode encryption.</solution>
<plugin_output>
  The following client-to-server CBC algorithms are supported :
    aes128-cbc
    aes256-cbc
</plugin_output>
</ReportItem>
</ReportHost>

