<ReportItem port="8080" svc_name="www" protocol="tcp" severity="4" pluginID="900104" pluginName="Apache Log4j Remote Code Execution (Log4Shell)" pluginFamily="Web Servers">
<plugin_type>remote</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>Critical</risk_factor>
<cvss3_base_score>10.0</cvss3_base_score>
<cvss3_vector>CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H</cvss3_vector>
<cvss_base_score>10.0</cvss_base_score>
<vpr_score>10.0</vpr_score>
<exploit_available>true</exploit_available>
<cve>CVE-2021-44228</cve>
<synopsis>The remote web application uses a library affected by a remote code execution vulnerability.</synopsis>
<description>The remote web application uses a version of Apache Log4j 2 that is affected by a remote code execution vulnerability in its JNDI lookup feature. Nessus confirmed the issue by sending a lookup string that causes a harmless DNS query and observing that query arrive.</description>
<solution>Upgrade Apache Log4j to version 2.17.1 or later.</solution>
<see_also>https://logging.apache.org/log4j/2.x/security.html</see_also>
<plugin_output>
  Nessus received a DNS lookup from the target after sending a crafted
  lookup string in the User-Agent header of a request to :
  URL : http://app01.example.test:8080/
</plugin_output>
</ReportItem>
